<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Comares Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Comares Palace is the official part of the Nasrid palaces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra">Alhambra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, built mainly under Yusuf I and Muhammad V in the fourteenth century. It is arranged around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/court-of-the-myrtles">Court of the Myrtles</a> with its long pool and dominated by the Comares Tower, which houses the Hall of the Ambassadors, the emir's throne room. Its walls carry carved stucco, tile dados and inscribed poetry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/comares-palace.jpg" alt="Comares Palace" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastian Appelt · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patio_de_los_Arrayanes_Alhambra_Spain_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
